0 ratings by Goodreads\n\n \n\nImage: 9780691168487: e: The Story of a Number (Princeton Science Library)\n\nSoftcover\n\nISBN 10: 0691168482 ISBN 13: 9780691168487\n\nPublisher: Princeton University Press, 2015\n\nView all copies of this ISBN edition\n\n13 Used From US$ 7.32\n\n23 New From US$ 14.14\n\n  * Synopsis\n  * About this title\n  * Edition details\n\n### Synopsis\n\nThe interest earned on a bank account, the arrangement of seeds in a sunflower, and the shape of the Gateway Arch in St. Louis are all intimately connected with the mysterious number e. In this informal and engaging history, Eli Maor portrays the curious characters and the elegant mathematics that lie behind the number. Designed for a reader with only a modest mathematical background, this biography brings out the central importance of e to mathematics and illuminates a golden era in the age of science.\n\n\"synopsis\" may belong to another edition of this title.\n\n### About the Author\n\nEli Maor is the author of Beautiful Geometry (with Eugen Jost), Venus in Transit, Trigonometric Delights, To Infinity and Beyond, and The Pythagorean Theorem: A 4,000-Year History (all Princeton).\n\n\"About this title\" may belong to another edition of this title.\n\nPublisher\n    Princeton University Press\nPublication date\n    2015\nLanguage\n    English\nISBN 10 \n    0691168482\nISBN 13 \n    9780691168487\nBinding\n    Paperback\nNumber of pages\n    227\nRating\n\n### Buy Used\n\nCondition: Good\n\nItem in good condition. Textbooks...\n\nView this item\n\nUS$ 7.32\n\nFree Shipping Learn more about shipping rates\nShips within U.S.A.\n\nAdd to basket\n\n### Buy New\n\nView this item\n\nUS$ 14.14\n\nUS$ 2.64 shipping Learn more about shipping rates\nShips within U.S.A.\n\nAdd to basket\n\nFree 30-day returns\n\n### Search results for e: The Story of a Number (Princeton Science Library)\n\nStock Image\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIron, Steam & Money (https://www.penguin.co.uk/books/413050/iron-steam-and-money-by-roger-osborne/9781845952129)\nciteturn274search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 12.4 years ago; Crawled: 4 weeks ago; \n\nImage: Book cover of Iron, Steam & Money by Roger Osborne\n\n# Iron, Steam & Money\n\nbyRoger Osborne\n\n## The Making of the Industrial Revolution\n\n## Format:\n\nPaperbackEbook\n\n## Buy the book from:\n\nAmazonBlackwellsBookshop.orgFoylesHiveTGJonesWaterstones\n\nIn late eighteenth-century Britain a handful of men brought about the greatest transformation in human history. Inventors, industrialists and entrepreneurs ushered in the age of powered machinery and the factory, and thereby changed the whole of human society, bringing into being new methods of social and economic organisation, new social classes, and new political forces. The Industrial Revolution also dramatically altered humanity's relation to the natural world and embedded the belief that change, not stasis, is the necessary backdrop for human existence.\n\n> ## Ably handling a mass of material, Osborne explores both the technological side of his subject and its human aspect\n> \n> Christopher Smith, UK Regional Press Syndication\n\n> ## Osborne fires [the Industrial Revolution] up with great gusto\n> \n> Iain Finlayson, The Times\n\n> ## Detailed and scholarly\n> \n> Steve Craggs, UK Regional Press Syndication\n\n> ## A truly rattling good yarn\n> \n> Jonathan Glancey, Country Life\n\n> ## Iron, Steam & Money is an engaging and enjoyable read, and Osborne’s clear prose and simple explanations provide shape and meaning to a concept that in many people’s minds remains a muddled memory from school days\n> \n> Emma Griffin, BBC History Magazine\n\n> ## Meaty and satisfying\n> \n> Peter Forbes, Independent (Radar)\n\n## About Roger Osborne\n\nRoger Osborne's work has provided a range of innovative insights into our views of the past, and how they inform the present. His previous books include The Floating Egg: Episodes 